/-!
# Lemma 08R2, items (3) and (4), and items (7) and (8) over an arbitrary ring

[Stacks, Tag 08R2] lists situations in which the cotangent complex `L_{B/A}` vanishes. Items
(1), (2), (5), (6) are `CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_weaklyEtale_unconditional`,
`CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_flat_of_bijective`,
`CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_etale_unconditional` and
`CommAlgCat.cotangentComplex_isZero_of_filtered_colimit`. This file adds the remaining ones.

* Item (3), `B = S⁻¹A`: a localization is flat and an epimorphism, so item (2) applies; this is
  `CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_localization` of
  `StacksFrontier.Cotangent.Localization`.
* Item (4), `A → B` unramified and flat: the source reduces it to item (1). The kernel of the
  multiplication `B ⊗_A B → B` is generated by an idempotent `e` (`Ω_{B/A} = 0` and the kernel is
  finitely generated), so the multiplication is the localization of `B ⊗_A B` at `1 - e`, hence
  flat; with `A → B` flat this is weak étaleness.
* Items (7) and (8) for a local ring `A_𝔭` of an arbitrary ring `A`: the henselization
  `A_𝔭 → B` has `L_{B/A_𝔭} = 0`
  (`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_unconditional`, the case of a
  local base), `L_{A_𝔭/A} = 0` by item (3), and the fundamental triangle of
  `A → A_𝔭 → B` (Proposition 08QX) gives `L_{B/A} = 0`.

## Main results

* `Algebra.WeaklyEtale.of_formallyUnramified_of_flat`: an essentially of finite type, formally
  unramified, flat algebra is weakly étale.
* `CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_isLocalization`: **[Stacks, Tag 08R2] item (3)**.
* `CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_unramified_of_flat`: **[Stacks, Tag 08R2] item
  (4)**.
* `CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_isHenselization_atPrime`: **[Stacks, Tag 08R2]
  items (7) and (8)**, for a henselization of a local ring `A_𝔭` of an arbitrary ring `A`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08R2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08R2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00UT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00UT), unramified ring maps.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08QX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08QX), the fundamental
  triangle.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u v

/-- **A flat unramified algebra is weakly étale.** Let `A → B` be essentially of finite type,
formally unramified and flat. Then the multiplication `B ⊗_A B → B` is flat, so `B` is weakly
étale over `A`.

The kernel `I` of the multiplication is finitely generated and `I / I² = Ω_{B/A} = 0`, so `I` is
generated by an idempotent `e`. The multiplication is surjective with kernel `(e)`, so it is the
localization of `B ⊗_A B` at the idempotent `1 - e`, and localizations are flat. -/
theorem Algebra.WeaklyEtale.of_formallyUnramified_of_flat (A B : Type*) [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Algebra.EssFiniteType A B] [Algebra.FormallyUnramified A B]
    [Module.Flat A B] : Algebra.WeaklyEtale A B where
  flat_lmul' := by
    obtain ⟨e, he, hsp⟩ : ∃ e, IsIdempotentElem e ∧ KaehlerDifferential.ideal A B = B ⊗[A] B ∙ e :=
      (Ideal.isIdempotentElem_iff_of_fg _ (KaehlerDifferential.ideal_fg A B)).mp <|
        (Ideal.cotangent_subsingleton_iff _).mp <| inferInstanceAs <| Subsingleton Ω[B⁄A]
    algebraize [(Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' A (S := B)).toRingHom]
    have hker : RingHom.ker (algebraMap (B ⊗[A] B) B) = Ideal.span {1 - (1 - e)} := by
      rw [sub_sub_cancel]
      exact hsp
    have hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap (B ⊗[A] B) B) := fun b =>
      ⟨b ⊗ₜ[A] 1, by simp [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra]⟩
    have : IsLocalization.Away (1 - e) B :=
      IsLocalization.away_of_isIdempotentElem he.one_sub hker hsurj
    exact IsLocalization.flat B (Submonoid.powers (1 - e))

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

namespace CommAlgCat

section Vanishing

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 08R2] item (3).** Let `S ⊂ A` be a multiplicative subset and let
`B = S⁻¹A`. Then `L_{B/A} = 0` in `D(B)`.

A localization is flat and an epimorphism, so this is item (2),
`CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_flat_of_bijective`, through
`CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_localization`. -/
@[stacks 08R2 "item (3) of the lemma, `B = S⁻¹A` for a multiplicative subset `S ⊂ A`, read as \
`IsLocalization S B`. NOTHING is carried: the source derives it from item (2), and so does this \
proof, through `CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_localization`, a localization being \
flat and an epimorphism. The localization hypothesis is load-bearing, being the only source of \
both"]
theorem isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_isLocalization (S : Submonoid A) [IsLocalization S B] :
    IsZero (cotangentComplexDerived.{u, u} A (CommAlgCat.of A B)) :=
  isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_localization A S B

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 08R2] item (4).** Let `A → B` be unramified and flat. Then `L_{B/A} = 0` in
`D(B)`.

Unramified is Mathlib's `Algebra.Unramified`, formally unramified and of finite type, which is
the source's definition (Stacks 00UT, through 00UU). A flat unramified algebra is weakly étale,
`Algebra.WeaklyEtale.of_formallyUnramified_of_flat`, so this is item (1). -/
@[stacks 08R2 "item (4) of the lemma, `A → B` unramified and flat: `Algebra.Unramified A B` \
(formally unramified and of finite type, which is Stacks 00UT by Stacks 00UU) together with \
`Module.Flat A B`. NOTHING is carried: the source derives it from item (1), and so does this \
proof — flatness and unramifiedness make the multiplication `B ⊗_A B → B` a localization at an \
idempotent, hence flat (`Algebra.WeaklyEtale.of_formallyUnramified_of_flat`), and item (1) is \
`CommAlgCat.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_weaklyEtale_unconditional`, whose triangle is \
Proposition 08QX. Both hypotheses are load-bearing"]
theorem isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_unramified_of_flat [Algebra.Unramified A B]
    [Module.Flat A B] :
    IsZero (cotangentComplexDerived.{u, u} A (CommAlgCat.of A B)) :=
  have : Algebra.WeaklyEtale A B := Algebra.WeaklyEtale.of_formallyUnramified_of_flat A B
  isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_weaklyEtale_unconditional A B

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 08R2] items (7) and (8).** Let `A` be a ring, `𝔭 ⊂ A` a prime, and let
`A_𝔭 → B` be a henselization of the local ring `A_𝔭` of `A` with residue field a prescribed
extension `κ(𝔭) ⊆ L`. Then `L_{B/A} = 0` in `D(B)`.

At `L = κ(𝔭)` this is item (7), a henselization of a local ring of `A`, and at `L = κ(𝔭)^sep`
it is item (8), a strict henselization. The fundamental triangle of `A → A_𝔭 → B`
(Proposition 08QX) has first vertex `L_{A_𝔭/A} ⊗^𝐋 B = 0` by item (3) and third vertex
`L_{B/A_𝔭} = 0` by the local case
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_unconditional`, so its middle vertex
`L_{B/A}` vanishes. -/
@[stacks 08R2 "items (7) and (8) of the lemma, at once, for an ARBITRARY ring `A`: `B` a \
henselization (`L = κ(𝔭)`, item (7)) or a strict henselization (`L = κ(𝔭)^sep`, item (8)) of \
the local ring `A_𝔭 = Localization.AtPrime 𝔭` of `A`, read as `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization` \
(Stacks 04GQ) with the `A`-algebra structure on `B` the composite `A → A_𝔭 → B`. NOTHING is \
carried: the triangle of `A → A_𝔭 → B` is Proposition 08QX, \
`CommAlgCat.exists_distTriang_fundamentalVertex`; its first vertex vanishes by item (3) and its \
third by `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_unconditional`, which is the \
source's route through items (5) and (6) over the local ring"]
theorem isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_isHenselization_atPrime (p : Ideal A) [p.IsPrime]
    (L : Type v) [Field L] [Algebra (IsLocalRing.ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p)) L]
    [IsLocalRing B] [Algebra (Localization.AtPrime p) B]
    [IsScalarTower A (Localization.AtPrime p) B]
    [IsLocalRing.IsHenselization (Localization.AtPrime p) L B] :
    IsZero (cotangentComplexDerived.{u, u} A (CommAlgCat.of A B)) := by
  obtain ⟨_, _, _, hT⟩ := exists_distTriang_fundamentalVertex.{u} A (Localization.AtPrime p) B
  refine Triangle.isZero₂_of_isZero₁₃ _ hT ?_ ?_
  · exact Functor.map_isZero _
      (isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_of_isLocalization A (Localization.AtPrime p) p.primeCompl)
  · exact IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isZero_cotangentComplexDerived_unconditional
      (R := Localization.AtPrime p) L

end Vanishing

end CommAlgCat

